    "solution_steps": [
      "Compute the joint bounding rectangle of every gray cell.",
      "Create a zero output and fill the complete gray bounding rectangle with color 5.",
      "For each non-gray color from 1 through 9, compute the bounding box of all its input cells.",
      "Intersect that color box with the gray rectangle and fill the intersection when it is nonempty.",
      "Apply colors in ascending numeric order, allowing later higher colors to overwrite earlier intersections."
    ],
    "source": "canonical.program_solution and canonical.written_solution",
    "target_status": "canonical_rule_expanded",
    "target_text": "Restore the complete bounding rectangle of the gray (5) region on a zero background. For every other present color, fill the intersection between its joint input bounding box and the gray rectangle. Process colors in ascending numeric order, so higher-numbered colors win overlaps; erase all content outside the gray rectangle."
